Now before we go further, we computed boarding times in earlier iterations of this dataset, but technically, boarding is only for people BOARDING waiting to go upstairs, ie, be admitted. So technically, the boarding times do not apply to the entire dataset, even though we "computed" them. I want to start by seeing what the different categories are for dispo and then we'll remove anything that wasn't a --> inpatient team.

We eventually came back to this and instead of just using what was marked as "Admitted", Professor Dresser went through all of the variations that came up in the vibe check and manually coded as whether they were admitted eventually or not.

